# --- Variant A: env-tag-column-alignment (44870 bytes) ---
# Paired with docs/ui/env-tag-column-alignment.md + issue #23.
# Option A: shared CSS Grid on the service-level wrapper so all .leaf-pair cells in the
# same service block align env-tag column 1 to a common width.

VARIANT-A-ENV-TAG-ALIGNMENT | Env-tag column alignment — Variant A: shared grid on .workflow-rows-service wrapper; column 1 sized to widest env-label in service block; eliminates per-.leaf-pair independent sizing bug | @docs/ui/mockups/env-tag-column-alignment-variant-a.html
VARIANT-A-INVARIANT | NFR-09 reflow invariant applies: env-tag column aligns across all workflow rows within a service block at any env-label length; no overlap with connector arrows or box content | @docs/ui/mockups/env-tag-column-alignment-variant-a.html

# --- Variant B: env-tag-column-alignment (43288 bytes) ---
# Paired with docs/ui/env-tag-column-alignment.md + issue #23.
# Option B: CSS subgrid propagation — .workflow-rows-service wrapper establishes a named
# grid line; each .leaf-pair participates as a subgrid column so env-tag column sizes
# propagate from the service container without an explicit wrapper grid.

VARIANT-B-ENV-TAG-ALIGNMENT | Env-tag column alignment — Variant B: CSS subgrid propagation; named grid lines on service wrapper; .leaf-pair cells participate as subgrid so env-tag column 1 is jointly sized across all rows without explicit row-count knowledge | @docs/ui/mockups/env-tag-column-alignment-variant-b.html
VARIANT-B-INVARIANT | NFR-09 reflow invariant applies: same reflow guarantee as Variant A but via subgrid mechanism; browser support requirement: Chrome 117+ / Firefox 71+ / Safari 16+ (subgrid was not universally available pre-2023; baseline check needed before SPA adoption) | @docs/ui/mockups/env-tag-column-alignment-variant-b.html
